 "metricsNote": "Earth reference = general adult clinical ranges, simplified for this prototype (illustrative cut-offs). Sleep: adults need 7 h or more; ISS crews average 6.09 h against 8.5 h scheduled (Barger et al. 2014). Mood: one low day (1–2) is at most 'Watch'; red needs 3 or more low days in a row (illustrative).",
 "zscore": {
  "minDays": 7,
  "maxDays": 14,
  "yellow": 2,
  "red": 3,
  "illustrative": true,
  "note": "Personal baseline = mean and standard deviation of the first 7–14 days. A deviation of 2 SD = yellow 'Watch', 3 SD = yellow 'Caution'. A deviation from the personal baseline alone never turns red: red ('Notify doctor') needs the value to be outside the reference red limit, or 3 SD from baseline and outside the reference green range (illustrative)."
 },
